# Antigravity Autonomous Engineering & Governance Rules
# Chakri Sheba Stabilization, Routing & Quality Gate Protocol

## Core Engineering Guardrails
1. Never assume a route, mutation, or layout works without terminal test validation.
2. Never bundle Public, User Dashboard, and Admin Dashboard logic in one patch.
3. Every UI modification must maintain mobile (375px) and desktop (1440px) structural integrity without hydration mismatch or overflow.
4. All internal links (anchors, router pushes, navigation items) must strictly match registered filesystem routes.

## Route Protection & RBAC
- Every dynamic route (`[id]`, `[slug]`, `[...slug]`) must have defensive null/undefined checks and graceful fallback redirection rather than unhandled 404 or 500 exceptions.
- Non-admin attempts to access `/admin` or admin API routes without valid credentials must be cleanly handled (redirect to login or unauthorized view, never throw an uncaught server exception).
- User dashboard routes (`/dashboard`, `/profile`, `/vault`, `/wallet`, `/applications`) must require active authentication or cleanly redirect unauthenticated users to `/login?redirect=...`.

## Zero-Broken-Commit Quality Gate
- Run `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`) before every commit. Zero TypeScript compilation errors are permitted.
- Preserve data integrity in `src/db/local_store.json`. Never wipe, corrupt, or truncate store collections.
- Terminal tests (Playwright E2E) must run headlessly and verify HTTP 200 and error-free console logs.

